   $q$Which detail explains why Nadia is winning "on paper"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Tobias offered her a draw quietly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"weak-evidence"},{"text":"Her team led the match 2.5 to 1.5.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-game-and-match"},{"text":"She won a pawn early and kept it.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Coach Kim had drilled the team all season.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She won a pawn early and kept it.$q$, $q$Being a pawn up is the material advantage that makes her position winning on paper. The team score describes the match, not her individual game.$q$, 'draft', '37cd2a2f-789d-5ae3-882f-1bcb1ddcd067')
