  ('90bcb05a-bc72-5090-b04b-ae2ba39c35b1', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-story-details-inference'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Which statement best captures what the final paragraph shows and what it leaves open?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Ruth does not know Kenji timed the race and stops by his seat only by chance.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-evidence"},{"text":"Ruth deliberately acknowledges Kenji, but exactly what she feels about his call is left unsaid.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Ruth is clearly angry that Kenji cost her an outright win and refuses to speak to him.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstated-inference"},{"text":"Ruth openly thanks Kenji for his honesty before walking off the bus with her team.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Ruth deliberately acknowledges Kenji, but exactly what she feels about his call is left unsaid.$q$, $q$She stops at his seat on purpose, almost speaks, and knocks twice, an acknowledgment without words, so her exact feeling stays unclear. Calling her "clearly angry" ignores that the gesture is not hostile, and she never says a word of thanks.$q$, 'draft', 'af5efd6f-5f04-5752-b0f7-8613cd7984a3')
