   $q$In context, what does Dr. Eze mean by "At least is not the same as equal to"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Fallen stakes should be left out of the field book entirely.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Two meters is too large a number to be believable for one summer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"Recording exactly two meters would understate a melt known only to exceed it.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Anjali measured the stake carelessly and must redo the measurement.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Recording exactly two meters would understate a melt known only to exceed it.$q$, $q$They know only that melt was more than two meters, so writing "2.0" would wrongly present a minimum as the actual value. She does record Stake 9 in the book, as "Fallen. Melt exceeded 2.0 m," so leaving it out is not her point.$q$, 'draft', '03ef8cd6-7294-5fa9-ad99-a5bca140ce10')
