  ('9a548529-835c-5f12-a98c-ff218b906ca5', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-word-parts'), null, 'easy',
   $q$The root bio means "life," and lumin means "light." What does it mean that each organism is "bioluminescent"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It is a living thing that produces its own light","is_correct":true},{"text":"It feeds on light from the sun during the day","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-first-root"},{"text":"It reflects moonlight that strikes the water","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"It can survive only in very warm water","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It is a living thing that produces its own light$q$, $q$Bio plus lumin describes light made by a living thing, and the passage says each organism produces "its own light through a chemical reaction." Reflected moonlight ignores that the light comes from the organism itself, and the bay is described as moonless.$q$, 'draft', 'e3c23a21-e91e-5e9a-bdfa-606154d2af13')
