   $q$The root equi means "equal," and libr comes from a word for "balance" or "scales." What does a boat keep when it keeps its "equilibrium"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A fast and constant stroke rate","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"A straight line through every bend","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"An equal number of rowers and coaches","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-second-root"},{"text":"A steady balance between its two sides","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A steady balance between its two sides$q$, $q$Equi plus libr means equal balance, and Adaeze warns that if "one side pulls harder than the other, we wobble." A fast stroke rate matters in the race, but the word itself names balance, not speed.$q$, 'draft', 'd0ad9405-d926-5787-b2f2-fa201e805e69')
