   $q$The prefix re- means "again," and viv means "to live." What did Adaeze's words do when they seemed to "revive" the crew?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They warned the rowers about the sandbar","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"They gave the tired rowers new energy","is_correct":true},{"text":"They reminded the rowers of a past race","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-second-root"},{"text":"They calmed the rowers so they could rest","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They gave the tired rowers new energy$q$, $q$To revive is to bring back to life, and right after her words "the stroke rate climbed, and the boat surged." Calming them to rest is the opposite of the renewed effort the passage describes.$q$, 'draft', 'd0ad9405-d926-5787-b2f2-fa201e805e69')
