   $q$The root tort means "to twist," and the suffix -uous means "full of." Which meaning of "tortuous" fits the race course, and why?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Very dangerous, because the inside channel had a sandbar","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Very long, because the course stretched over three miles","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"Full of twists and turns, because the river bends sharply six times","is_correct":true},{"text":"Extremely painful, because the rowers became exhausted","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-similar-word"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Full of twists and turns, because the river bends sharply six times$q$, $q$Tort plus uous means full of twists, and the passage says the river "twisted through six sharp bends." "Extremely painful" confuses tortuous with the similar-looking word torturous.$q$, 'draft', 'd0ad9405-d926-5787-b2f2-fa201e805e69')
