        '3-5', $q$How Animals Get Through Winter$q$, $q$(1) Winter is a hard time for many animals. (2) The weather is cold, and food is hard to find. (3) Animals have different ways to get through the winter.

(4) One way is to move to a warmer place. (5) Many geese fly south in the fall to find food and warmer weather. (6) ___ way is to grow a thick winter coat. (7) A snowshoe hare grows thick white fur that keeps it warm and helps it hide in the snow.

(8) Some animals sleep through the cold months. (9) Woodchucks go into a deep sleep in their burrows. (10) A burrow is a hole or tunnel that an animal digs in the ground for a home. (11) While woodchucks sleep, their hearts beat much more slowly than usual. (12) My cat likes to sleep on a warm blanket all day.$q$, 'draft')
